invariant: INV-17
file: src/sha3.c
catches: sha3_equiv_test
reason: shake_absorb takes an absorb that fills its block to the last byte
  for one that runs no permutation, so it skips the wipe after the one
  absorb length at which the permutation starts to run. The lanes the
  compiler wrote to stack slots of its own stay there. bin/sha3_equiv_test
  makes that call and finds a lane it computed in the stack below it
  (docs/decisions.md 219).

--- old
    int permutes = n >= s->rate - s->pos;
--- new
    int permutes = n > s->rate - s->pos;
